   "subject": "Help Finding ESW",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello! I am running a Distance analysis using R and I am not sure how to find the effective strip width results. Am I missing them in the summary page? I would like to use the ESW for splitting my transects into segments for dsm.<div><br></div><div>Thanks for the help!</div><div><div><br></div><div>Sarah</div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "Yml0kHbOEgAJ",
   "from": "Eric Rexstad",
   "author": "f2122b34f1aa6e95",
   "date": "2015-11-13T15:51:42Z",
   "subject": "Re: [distance-sampling] Help Finding ESW",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n  \r\n    \r\n  \r\n  <div bgcolor=\"#FFFFFF\" text=\"#000000\">\r\n    <div>\r\n      <p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">Sarah:</p>\r\n      <p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">ESW is not printed\r\n        in the summary output of the Distance package. However, ESW is\r\n        defined as <img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/distance-sampling/attach/12ce7690746962/chart?part=0.1.1&amp;view=1\" alt=\"w*p_a\">,<br>\r\n        where w=perpendicular truncation distance and <img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/distance-sampling/attach/12ce7690746962/chart?part=0.1.2&amp;view=1\" alt=\"p_a\">=probability\r\n        of detection given object is within covered region.</p>\r\n      <p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">You know w (from\r\n        your data) and Distance provides <img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/distance-sampling/attach/12ce7690746962/chart?part=0.1.2&amp;view=1\" alt=\"p_a\">,\r\n        so you can calculate ESW</p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div bgcolor=\"#FFFFFF\" text=\"#000000\"><div>\r\n      <p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">On 13/11/2015 15:05,\r\n        Sarah Moore wrote:</p>\r\n      <p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"></p>\r\n      </div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div bgcolor=\"#FFFFFF\" text=\"#000000\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\">\r\n          \r\n          <div dir=\"ltr\">Hello! I am running a Distance analysis using R\r\n            and I am not sure how to find the effective strip width\r\n            results. Am I missing them in the summary page? I would like\r\n            to use the ESW for splitting my transects into segments for\r\n            dsm.\r\n            <div><br>\r\n            </div>\r\n            <div>Thanks for the help!</div>\r\n            <div>\r\n              <div><br>\r\n              </div>\r\n              <div>Sarah</div>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
